[38;5;231m⏺[39m Recorded: global script tag.

  [1mNext: the shape of what [38;5;153msettings.js[39m exports.[0m Right now the constant is a full URL with the path baked in
  ([38;5;153mhttps://api.example.com/login[39m). Once it's per-environment, that choice decides how the second endpoint gets added.

  - [1mBase URL + paths built in code[0m — [38;5;153mSETTINGS.apiBaseUrl = "https://api.example.com"[39m, and [38;5;153mlogin()[39m builds [38;5;153m${base}/login[39m.
    Adding an endpoint later is a one-line change in the calling code; the environment map stays one entry per
    environment.
  - [1mFull endpoint URLs per environment[0m — keep [38;5;153mloginUrl[39m as a complete URL in each environment block. Dead simple and lets
    one environment point somewhere odd, but every new endpoint multiplies by the number of environments.

  [1mMy recommendation: base URL + paths in code.[0m With three environments, the full-URL version means editing three places
  to add one endpoint, and the per-environment freedom it buys is not something this app needs. It's also cheap to
  reverse — the map is a few lines either way.

